<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================
  cr-dotnet-0010 : Web.config Transformations — REMEDIATED
  ============================================================
  This Web.Release.config transformation file has been superseded
  by runtime environment variable injection and AWS Systems Manager
  Parameter Store, following the 12-factor app configuration principle.

  PREVIOUS APPROACH (build-time, cloud-incompatible):
    XDT transformations baked environment-specific values into the
    build artifact, preventing immutable deployments and making it
    impossible to promote the same artifact across environments.
    The <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" /> directive
    was used to strip the debug flag at release build time — this is now
    handled by the ASPNET_ENV / DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT runtime variable.

  CLOUD-NATIVE REPLACEMENT (runtime, AWS-compatible):
    All environment-specific configuration is now injected at runtime
    via the following mechanisms (in priority order):

    1. Environment Variables (highest priority)
       Set these in your AWS deployment environment (ECS task definition,
       Elastic Beanstalk environment properties, App Runner service, etc.):

         DB_CONNECTION_STRING
           The full ADO.NET connection string for the application database.
           Example: "Server=mydb.cluster-xyz.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com;
                     Database=tourdb;User Id=appuser;Password=<secret>;"

         S3_TOUR_PICS_BUCKET
           The S3 bucket name for tour image uploads.
           Example: "tour-management-tour-pics-prod"

         CSP_POLICY
           Optional override for the Content-Security-Policy header value.

         CLOUDFRONT_CDN_HOST
           Optional CloudFront distribution domain for CDN script delivery.

         ASPNET_ENV
           Controls debug/release behaviour at runtime.
           Set to "Production" to disable debug compilation output.
           Equivalent to the former <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)"/>.

    2. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (fallback)
       Parameters are resolved at application startup via the
       AwsSsmHelper utility class when the corresponding environment
       variable is absent:

         /tour-management/db-connection-string   → DB_CONNECTION_STRING
         /tour-management/s3-tour-pics-bucket    → S3_TOUR_PICS_BUCKET

       Use AWS Secrets Manager for sensitive values (passwords, API keys)
       and reference them from Parameter Store using SecureString parameters.

    3. Web.config appSettings / connectionStrings (lowest priority / local dev only)
       The values in Web.config serve as last-resort defaults for local
       development only and must NOT contain production credentials.

  MIGRATION NOTES:
    - Web.Debug.config and Web.Release.config XDT transforms are no longer
      applied during the build pipeline.
    - The <compilation debug="true"> attribute is controlled by the
      ASPNET_ENV / DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT environment variable at runtime.
    - Connection strings are never baked into build artifacts.
    - Secrets are stored in AWS Secrets Manager and referenced via
      Parameter Store SecureString parameters — never in config files.
  ============================================================
-->
<configuration>
  <!--
    No XDT transformations are defined here.
    All environment-specific configuration is injected at runtime
    via environment variables and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.
    See the comment block above for the full configuration reference.
  -->
</configuration>
